=== OCC exercise-by-exception ($0.01 in-the-money, unless contrary instructions) ===
  call K=100 close=100.01 ITM=0.01 -> exception exercise? True
  call K=100 close=100.0 ITM=0.0 -> exception exercise? False
  call K=100 close=99.99 ITM=-0.01 -> exception exercise? False
  put K=100 close=99.99 ITM=0.01 -> exception exercise? True
  put K=100 close=100.0 ITM=0.0 -> exception exercise? False
  put K=100 close=100.01 ITM=-0.01 -> exception exercise? False
a clearing member may still instruct OCC not to exercise an ITM option, or to exercise one that is below the threshold
this procedure is between OCC and clearing members; a broker may use a different customer threshold
=== Assignment creates a stock position (standard 100-share equity contract) ===
writer assigned on 1 call: stock position -100 shares
writer assigned on 1 put: stock position 100 shares
those stock trades settle T+1 after exercise; a backtest that 'expires worthless' every option will miss this inventory
=== OCC assignment is random at the clearing level; the customer method is the firm's ===
OCC assigns exercise notices to clearing-member accounts at random (OIC Assignment FAQ)
the assigned firm then uses an exchange-approved method (usually random or FIFO); a fair method, not necessarily random
one assignment using FIFO at the firm -> allocated to customer A (opened 2026-11-02)
short closed during today's trading hours; net short after the close=0 -> assigned tonight? False
do not invent a single official retail OCC customer cutoff such as 5:30 p.m.; ask the firm
assertions passed: 9/9
